# EXAMNIA Phase 7 - rate limits and private API responses.
# No new endpoints are introduced. These examples exercise existing routes.
# See phase-7-hardening.md for every budget, HTTPS/proxy configuration, and deployment steps.
# Run against your local development API; the changes do not require local HTTPS.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
@studentToken = PASTE_STUDENT_LOGIN_DATA_TOKEN
@teacherToken = PASTE_TEACHER_LOGIN_DATA_TOKEN
@classId = PASTE_CLASS_ID_OWNED_BY_THIS_TEACHER

### Student login - 200; use only locally seeded demo credentials.
# Inspect Cache-Control: no-store, private; X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff;
# X-Frame-Options: DENY; Referrer-Policy: no-referrer.
# Copy data.token into studentToken. Never share this token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student1@example.test",
  "password": "DemoPassword123!",
  "device_name": "phase-seven-student"
}

### Account request budget - 200 until the shared allowance is exhausted.
# Default: 120 authenticated requests/minute/account across tokens and route IDs.
# For a short LOCAL demonstration, set API_RATE_PER_MINUTE=2 and run
# php artisan config:clear, then repeat this GET until 429. Restore the default afterward.
# Other authenticated calls made during the same window also consume that allowance.
# A 429 includes error.code=TOO_MANY_REQUESTS, error.details={}, Retry-After,
# and rate-limit headers. Wait the returned number of seconds before retrying.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### No token - 401 even if an account previously reached its limit.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json

### Wrong role - 403; students cannot consume teacher functionality.
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/gradebook
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Teacher gradebook - 200; account-wide report and general API budgets both apply.
# Set teacherToken using the login example in phase-3-api.http.
# Default report budget: 30 requests/minute/account, shared across gradebooks,
# quiz grades, personal grades, and authorized completed reviews.
# A policy denial after the role check also counts; changing IDs does not reset a budget.
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/gradebook
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Malformed email - 422 validation response rather than a limiter conversion error.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": [],
  "password": "not-a-real-password",
  "device_name": "phase-seven-input-check"
}

### Unknown API resource - 404, same JSON error envelope and private response headers.
GET {{baseUrl}}/missing-phase-seven-resource
Accept: application/json

### Allowed frontend preflight - 204 with CORS and API security headers.
# Replace Origin with your configured FRONTEND_ORIGINS value when needed.
# Retry-After / rate-limit response headers are exposed to allowed browser origins.
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:4173
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

# Full endpoint examples remain in phase-1-api.http, phase-3-api.http,
# phase-4-api.http, phase-5-api.http, and phase-6-api.http.
# Generation requests have separate 3/minute and 20/hour limits; the ordinary
# generation status GET uses the general account budget. Existing jobs are unaffected by 429.
